  "analysis": "Both responses outline lanes, approvals, and rollback, but ZNX offers a more pragmatic mitigation of the known CI timeout issue by sharding the visual regression suite and allowing a warning instead of a hard failure, matching the repository fact that manual retries are common. It also provides a phased rollout, explicit timeline, and detailed cross‑team audit, reducing likely follow‑up questions. TVS is stricter (no timeout waivers) and lacks those practical mitigations.",
